WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.188
Lab 1 needs only a laptop with PowerShell
7 and Pester; no tenant, no network.

2
00:00:06.188 --> 00:00:09.563
First you run Microsoft's own
samples against the fakes.

3
00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:14.056
Find the test that creates a credential
with Graph's sample and then exchanges

4
00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:18.412
a token with a different subject: the
create succeeds and the exchange fails.

5
00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:20.775
That's the whole risk, in one test.

6
00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:25.140
Then you list what each task needs,
and build the plan from the fixtures:

7
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.752
eight conversions in two waves,
two failed exchange tests,

8
00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:31.837
and twenty actions, of
which only four would write.

9
00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:34.940
The plan's hash is the same on every run.
